course: dictionary
lesson: 12690
title: Diversification: making things more varied
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Diversification means making something more varied by adding different kinds of things. It comes from diverse, which means different or varied. The ending -ation turns the action into a noun, so diversify is the doing and diversification is the act of doing it.
explain: «The village shop sold only bread, so the owner started selling fruit, cheese and flowers.» The shop is now more varied because it has added different kinds of things. That is diversification. Check it: swap in your meaning and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Money and business use the word too. «The family put their savings into shares, houses and gold, not just one bank account.» Spreading money across many areas is diversification, and it lowers the risk that one thing going wrong will ruin everything.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Phrases like «more varied», «many areas» and «different kinds» point to its meaning. Words like «started» or «added» show that a change is happening.
fact: Diversification is a noun. «A diversification» is one change, and «diversification» on its own names the idea.
fact: «Diversification» means the act of making something more varied by adding different kinds of things.
fact: In money and business, «diversification» means spreading money, work or products across many different areas to reduce risk.
fact: «Diversification of crops» means a farmer grows different kinds of crop instead of only one.
fact: «Diversification of the economy» means a town or country does not depend on just one industry.
exercise: The village shop started selling fruit, cheese and flowers as well as bread. What word describes this change? | Hibernation | *Diversification | Punctuation | Exhaustion
exercise: What does «diversification of crops» mean? | Selling the farm to a bank | Stopping all farming | *Growing many different kinds of crop | Growing only one crop for years
exercise: In money and business, what does diversification do to risk? | *Reduces it by spreading money across many areas | Doubles the money you have | Makes it certain to happen | Increases it a lot
test: «The family put their savings into shares, houses and gold.» What is the family doing? | Losing their savings | Spending everything in one shop | *Spreading their money across many areas | Hiding money under a bed
test: In «a diversification», what kind of word is diversification? | *A noun | A full stop | A verb | An adjective
exam: Which sentence uses diversification correctly? | The diversification was a loud noise at night. | The farm grew only one crop, which was diversification. | *The town's diversification of jobs means it no longer depends on one factory. | Diversification is the colour of the sky.
